                  %a{:href => "#from_mbranes_to_fbranes"} From M-branes to F-branes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reduction_of_membrane_to_string"} Reduction of membrane to string
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reduction_of_m5brane_to_d4brane"} Reduction of M5-brane to D4-brane
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reduction_of_black_m2s_and_black_m5s"} Reduction of black M2s and black M5s
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reduction_of_mwaves_and_mk6s"} Reduction of M-Waves and MK6s
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em double dimensional reduction
            is a variant of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} Kaluza-Klein mechanism
            combined with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            in the presence of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            in which a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            propagates, its KK-reduction results in a
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            = succeed "-brane," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
            the cycle along which the KK-reduction takes place.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#via_fiber_integration_in_ordinary_differential_cohomology Via fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1 \in \mathbb{N}
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{p+1}U(1)_{conn} \in \mathbf{H}
            for the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            (given by the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
          %p
            Notice that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
            has the following stacky incarnation (see
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology#ViaSmoothHomotopyType"} here
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leq p+1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              is reflected by a morphism of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∫
                                  %mi Σ
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi Σ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi curv
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi curv
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∫
                                  %mi Σ
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                                %mo −
                                %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [\Sigma, \mathbf{B}^{p+1}U(1)_{conn}]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\int_\Sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^{p+1-k}U(1)_{conn}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{[\Sigma,curv]} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{curv}
                    \\\
                    [\Sigma,\mathbf{\Omega}^{p+2}]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\int_\Sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^{p+2-k}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the vertical morphisms are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              maps and the bottom morphisms reflects ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
          #DoubleDimensionalReductionForDifferentialCocycles.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\nabla \;\colon\; X \times \Sigma \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^{p+1}U(1)_{conn}
                    \\,,
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %em double dimensional reduction
              is the cocycle on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which is given by the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ∇
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi Σ
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \longrightarrow [\Sigma, X \times \Sigma]
                    \\stackrel{[\Sigma,\nabla]}{\longrightarrow}
                    [\Sigma,\mathbf{B}^{p+1}U(1)_{conn}]
                    \\stackrel{\int_\Sigma}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{B}^{p+1-k}U(1)_{conn}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first morphism is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              of the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              = succeed ")-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          %h3#ViaCyclicLoopSpaces Via cyclic loop spaces
          %p
            We discuss here a formalization of double dimensional reduction via cyclification adjunction (
            %a{:href => "#FSS16"}> FSS 16, section 3
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BMSS18"} BMSS 18, section 2.2
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes#DoubleDimensionalReduction"} section on double dimensional reduction
          #GeneralReduction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              along the canonical point inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbf{B}G
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              takes the following form: There is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%E2%88%9E-functors"} adjoint ∞-functors
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi hofib
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{[G,-]/G}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{hofib}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]/G
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                  by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  equipped with its canonical
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
                  by left multiplication and the argument regarded as equipped with its trivial
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed "-action" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = S^1
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  this is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space"} cyclic loop space
                  construction).
            %p Hence for
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to X
                  a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
                  object, such as for some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %p
              then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext original
                        %mrow
                          %mtext fluxes
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi oxidation
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi reduction
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
