          %h3#reduction_of_membrane_to_string Reduction of membrane to string
          %p
            The concept of double dimensional reduction was introduced, for the case of the reduction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermembrane"} supermembrane
            in 11d to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            in 10d, in
          %ul
            %li#DuffHoweInamiStelle87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 10
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                  from Supermembranes in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
              (ed.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
              205-206 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245249"}> spire:245249
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2
          %p
            The above “brane scan” table showing the double dimensional reduction pattern of the super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-branes given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            (see there for more references on this) is taken from
          %ul
            %li#Duff
